meta {
  name: 01 Get Date Filter Default
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/user-preferences/date-filters/{{dateFilterScreenKey}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  dateFilterScreenKey: registration-billings
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  The signed-in user's own saved **default date filter** for one list screen
  (the "Default date filter" pop-up). Login-only (no permission key); tenant and
  person come from the JWT, so a user can only ever read their own default.

  `:screenKey` — one of:
  - `registration-billings` (Registration › Billings)
  - `finance-billings` (Finance › Billings)
  - `registration-order-console` (Registration › Order Console)
  - `accession-inhouse-orders` (Accession › In-House Orders)
  - `accession-referral-orders` (Accession › Internal Referral Orders)
  - `technician-reporting` (Technician › Reporting)
  Anything else → 400 `USER_PREFERENCE_INVALID_SCREEN`.

  ONE default per user per screen — it applies to every tab of that screen.

  Response `data`: `null` when nothing is saved (the screen opens on the last 15 days), else
  `{ screenKey, preset, dateFrom, dateTo, updatedAt }`. `preset` is a relative
  range (`TODAY`, `YESTERDAY`, `LAST_7_DAYS`, `LAST_15_DAYS`, `LAST_30_DAYS`,
  `THIS_MONTH`)
  resolved by the frontend against the business day each time the screen opens,
  or `CUSTOM` with fixed `dateFrom`/`dateTo` (`YYYY-MM-DD`; null otherwise).
}
